---
description: Project architecture and engineering standards
alwaysApply: true
---

Project Stack:
- React frontend
- Express.js backend
- MongoDB database
- JWT authentication
- Bootstrap UI

Architecture:
- MVC + Service Layer architecture
- Controllers only handle request/response
- Business logic belongs in services
- Models only manage schema/data logic
- Frontend separated into pages/components/hooks/services
- API-first development

Backend Standards:
- RESTful API design
- Use async/await consistently
- Centralized error handling
- Validation middleware before controllers
- Do not access database directly inside controllers
- Use modular folder structure
- Keep services loosely coupled

Frontend Standards:
- Reusable components
- Avoid duplicated UI logic
- Separate API calls into service layer
- Keep components focused and small
- Responsive design required

Engineering Rules:
- Prefer incremental safe edits
- Avoid unnecessary refactors
- Preserve existing functionality
- Explain risky changes before implementing
- Read related files before modifying code
- Do not generate placeholder code unless requested

Testing Expectations:
- Consider edge cases
- Validate API responses
- Avoid regressions
- Verify loading/error states in UI